            <ArticleTitle>Nonstoichiometric Cux Iny S Quantum Dots for Efficient Photocatalytic Hydrogen Evolution.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>4833-4838</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/cssc.201701950</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Unlike their bulk counterpart, Cux Iny S quantum dots (QDs) prepared by an aqueous synthetic approach, show promising activity for photocatalytic hydrogen evolution, which is competitive with the state-of-the-art Cd chalcogen QDs. Moreover, the as-prepared Cux Iny S QDs with In-rich composition show much better efficiency than the stoichiometric ones (Cu/In=1:1).</AbstractText>
